Fail when the -t tries run out on a body cut short.
When the connection kept closing before the end of the body and the
tries ran out, wget kept the partial file, went on to the next URL and
exited with status 0, so a script could not tell an incomplete download
from a complete one. Resolve the FIXME there by failing with "giving
up", like every other error that ends a download. The partial file is
kept, as before, so -c can continue it.

---
 networking/wget.c |    4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/networking/wget.c
+++ b/networking/wget.c
@@ -1634,8 +1634,8 @@
 				G.beg_range += G.transferred;
 				goto restart;
 			}
-			/* else: -t TRIES exceeded */
-//FIXME: should we abort instead of continuing with next URL?
+			/* -t TRIES exceeded */
+			bb_simple_error_msg_and_die("giving up");
 		}
 		if (!(option_mask32 & WGET_OPT_OUTNAME)) {
 			xclose(G.output_fd);
